# Sensitive material — pre-flight checklist

Pre-flight checklist for any outward-facing material, ordered by severity.
**This page records the WHY so future sessions do not resurrect dropped
claims.** That sentence is the whole point of the file: without the reasoning,
a later session re-derives a claim someone already decided to kill.

Items are numbered so a review can cite `B4` and mean one specific thing.

---

## A. Never repeat

Factually unsupported, fabricated, or materially misleading. A hit here is a
stop-the-line defect, not a judgment call.

Format per item: the claim in bold, where it appeared, why it fails, the
registry IDs involved.

*(empty at bootstrap; filled by the prior-material sweep and the claim audit)*

---

## B. Reframe required

True-ish but wrongly framed. Each item states the reality **and the exact
permitted formulation**. An item without a permitted formulation is not
finished.

### Starter list: generic exposure classes

These apply to any company. **Confirm or delete each one before the first
build**, and a deletion needs one line of why. Deleting them all is a decision;
leaving them unreviewed is not.

| # | Exposure | Required reframe |
|---|---|---|
| B1 | Unqualified superlative ("leading", "first", "only", "best") | Add scope, metric, and source, or delete |
| B2 | Undated number | Stamp the period on the face |
| B3 | Unit-less number | State the unit and the currency |
| B4 | Forward target stated as fact | "target" / "plan", with safe-harbour framing |
| B5 | Market size without analyst and vintage | Name the analyst and the report date |
| B6 | Growth rate off a small base | State the absolute base beside the rate |
| B7 | Adjusted or non-GAAP figure alone | Show the statutory figure and one line of reconciliation |
| B8 | Rank claim without scope and share | State the ranking basis and the actual share |
| B9 | An LOI, MOU, or framework framed as a closed deal | Use the announcement's own language, including its caveats |
| B10 | An investor or backer named to imply more than the instrument | Name the actual instrument, amount, and date |
| B11 | Customer logos or named individuals | Written consent, or render as anonymised text |
| B12 | Third-party trademarks | Cleared rights, or set type instead of the mark |
| B13 | Competitor named and disparaged | Source it, date it, neutralise it, or drop it |
| B14 | Health, efficacy, or clinical claim on a non-medical product | Drop the claim; keep the product description |
| B15 | Pricing that contradicts the live site | Date-label the pricing basis |
| B16 | Headcount, facility, or location count | Date-stamp it; counts drift monthly |
| B17 | Capability claim beyond what ships today | Describe what exists; put the rest on a roadmap |
| B18 | Data-scale claim ("millions of records") | Use the sourced language verbatim |
| B19 | Regulatory or legal history | Know it cold; decide consciously whether the deck raises it |
| B20 | Unlicensed stock or AI-generated imagery | Replace with owned or licensed assets |

---

## C. Deliberately soft-pedalled

Known, framed consciously. Flag a slide only when it **crosses the stated
boundary**, not because the topic appears.

This list cannot be automated. It comes from one question, asked of the person
who owns the deck:

> *What must this deck never say, and what will an investor raise that we would
> rather not raise ourselves?*

*(empty at bootstrap; fill from that answer before the storyboard gate)*

---

## D. Polish defects

Mechanical, fix in any successor. Leftover source-language text on a
translated slide, a label that contradicts its own footnote, a duplicate
slide, a watermark, an undated column, a unit-less number.

---

## How an unreviewed item behaves

While `status: bootstrap`, an item nobody has ruled on behaves as **class C**
during a sweep: flagged only if the slide crosses its boundary. That makes the
first sweep on a new deck noisier than a mature one, and it quiets as items get
ruled into A, B, C, or deleted. This is expected. Track the ruling rate in the
review record; flip `status` to `reviewed` when the starter list has been
walked.
